<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_Desert                                     UtinniPatches - authored 2026-09-09
    BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1. Full sheet: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/desert.md
    (FROZEN, BIOME_FREEZE_FABLE_REVIEW_1). Replaces the donor Desert (vanilla Core,
    currently retextured/weather-patched by GRiNDTerra Terrain Retexture and others) —
    own def, not a patch, same reasoning as RUT_BlueDesert: sheet-governed weather,
    plantDensity and terrain are patch targets today (`biome_flora.py`,
    `BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml`, and third-party retexture patches all touch this donor
    def); a def we author stops being a patch collision.

    MEASURED (sheet SS0): arc 60-88 deg (sun 14.4 deg above horizon), temp median
    25.5 C, hilliness 2.0. Tile count is not restated here — it is repainted by
    world edits and drifts; read it live from `world/ASHKARR_WORLDMAP_tiles.csv`.
    Sheet's thematic handle: "the long shade" —
    shade is patchy, permanent and never moves; nothing here pursues (ban 3); nothing
    is nocturnal (ban 1, no day/night geometry to key off).

    plantDensity dropped to vanilla's own 0.05 (not the 0.45 a terrain-retexture patch
    currently carries): ban 8 is explicit — "vegetation meagre and never green in
    quantity." terrainsByFertility kept at vanilla Sand/Soil rather than the donor's
    patched NewAridSoil (a GRiNDTerra Terrain Retexture def) — no MayRequire needed,
    and nothing in the sheet asks for a different soil.

    Weather: ban 2 is a hard ban on rain here (R-H1; only the peaks and the river
    margin are exempt, and this is neither) — Rain/RainyThunderstorm zeroed. Snow
    zeroed too: not a named ban, but "the heat never breaks... never a cold night"
    (SS4 "Never a cold night") reads badly against a snow entry, so it is dropped as a
    thematic call, distinct from the hard ban, and flagged as such here rather than
    silently. DryThunderstorm and Sandstorm (Odyssey) kept — "the smoke is a gift"
    (ash/dust events fit; SS4). GrayPall (Anomaly) kept per the standard MayRequire
    pattern already used on RUT_BlueDesert/RUT_TheScald.

    wildAnimals/wildPlants: transplanted from BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml /
    BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml (see specs.py header) — both generated against
    rosters/desert.json, which is this sheet's own landed fauna/flora pass
    (BIOME_FAUNA_ASSIGNMENT_SITTING_1, 2026-09-09).

    foragedFood: DESERT_FORAGEDFOOD_INERT_1 (2026-09-20). The donor's RawAgave points
    at Plant_Agave, which desert.json's flora_purged list explicitly cuts as
    Earth-nameable, so the donor value was never carried forward — but leaving
    foragedFood unset makes forageability 0.25 inert (MEASURED: engine's
    GetForagedFoodCountPerInterval returns 0 with no foragedFood set, regardless of
    forageability). Set to RSW_RawHubbaGourd, the wild hubba gourd's own harvested
    item (RSW_Plant_HubbaGourd_Wild is already in this def's own wildPlants list) —
    MayRequire-guarded to match every other mandrake.rsw.swbestiary reference in this
    file, since that mod is only a loadAfter here, not a hard modDependency.
    wildPlantsCareAboutLocalFertility/lakeBeachTerrain added to match vanilla Core
    Desert's own fields, absent from this def until now.

    NOT this pass's scope: painting this def onto the world (a separate live-bridge
    step, `BLUE_DESERT_WORLD_SWITCH_1`'s own template); burst-predator staged
    statFactors and filter-feeding megafauna (both SS10/SS4c "Owed" — design and
    art not authored here).

    DESERT_SIGNATURE_FLORA_1 (2026-09-20): the ultracactus (§4b/§7) now has a def
    (RSW_Ultracactus, RSW_ExtremeDesertSignatureFlora.xml's neighbour
    RSW_Ultracactus.xml) and is wired into wildPlants below — the note above that
    it was undefined is now false and was corrected in this commit.
    DESERT_SHADE_PLANTS_DESIGN_1 designed §4b's two "shade plants, which defend"
    and CLOSED (417c7f516, 2026-09-20): two plants, not three, built by its two
    successors, VENOMVINE_CONTACT_VENOM_BUILD_1 (tier c) and
    DESERT_LEACHMOSS_BUILD_1 (tier b). Cite those, not the closed parent.

    DESERT_STAGGERSEED_BUILD_1 (2026-09-20): the cycle plant (§4b "The seed that
    uses you", §7 "the prepared cycle-seed") now has both its ThingDefs and both
    its mechanisms — RUT_Vorrel / RUT_VorrelFruit /
    RUT_VorrelSeedDish in mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora, driven by
    RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_HediffComp_ShadeStagger — and is wired into
    wildPlants below. The shade-grid MapComponent it reads
    (RM_MapComponent_ShadeGrid) also landed, under DESERT_SHADE_GRID_KEYSTONE_1;
    the older note above listing both as Owed was false and was corrected here.
    ⚠️ The plant still ships under its WORKING name — the shipping name is the
    owner's pick (§4b) and the card is items/STAGGERSEED_SHIPPING_NAME_1.md, so
    every RUT_Vorrel* defName in this file and in AshkarrFlora is provisional
    until it returns.

    DESERT_LEACHMOSS_BUILD_1 (2026-09-20, this pass): the moss half of §4b's
    "shade plants, which defend" pair now has a def (RM_Leachmoss,
    mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards,
    src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/RM_Leachmoss.xml)
    and is wired into wildPlants below at the highest weight in the list, per
    the design's own spawn-competition numbers
    (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/desert_shade_plants_design.md §2b).

    VENOMVINE_CONTACT_VENOM_BUILD_1 (2026-09-20): the vine half of that pair —
    the one that "holds territory by injury" — now has a def (RM_Venomvine,
    mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards,
    src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/RM_Venomvine.xml)
    and is wired into wildPlants below at 0.25. Its mechanism is
    RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.CompContactVenom +
    MapComponent_ContactVenom: one RM_VenomvineScratch on first contact, then
    one per in-game hour of lingering, carrying the RM_VenomvineVenom hediff.
    Flyers and races carrying the ContactVenomImmunity extension are untouched,
    and the whole mechanism sits behind a Mod Setting. Both this and the moss
    ship in the RM hazards kit rather than beside RSW_Ultracactus because a
    defName must carry its own mod's tier prefix and neither plant is Star Wars
    content. The pair is complete; nothing of §4b's shade plants remains owed.

  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_Desert</defName>
    <label>the Desert</label>
    <description>A dayside band of scattered rock at a sun so low every stone throws a shadow four times its own height. Nothing lives in the light and nothing survives leaving shelter, so life here is a sprint between islands of shade -- rest, dash, rest -- and the gaps between them are the only geography that matters. Cooler and steadier than the deep dune beyond it: the numbers are small, but they hold.</description>
    <workerClass>RimWorld.BiomeWorker_Desert</workerClass>

    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>false</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>0.4</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.05</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.25</forageability>
    <foragedFood MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_RawHubbaGourd</foragedFood>
    <wildPlantsCareAboutLocalFertility>false</wildPlantsCareAboutLocalFertility>
    <lakeBeachTerrain>Sand</lakeBeachTerrain>
    <movementDifficulty>1</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>World/Biomes/Desert</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>90</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalFlu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalPlague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_OrganDecay</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>10</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>Sand</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.8</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>Soil</terrain>
        <min>0.8</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>90</Clear>
      <DryThunderstorm>4</DryThunderstorm>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
      <GrayPall MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">1</GrayPall>
      <Sandstorm MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">4</Sandstorm>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <RSW_Bantha MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.8</RSW_Bantha>  <!-- bantha - huge-herd, adjust-keep -->
      <!-- ECOSYSTEM_PYRAMID_LAW_1 (owner, 2026-09-20: "50% small"): this roster read
           45.0% small, the biggest roster in the sweep. JOE_Landopus is already an
           OWNER-RULED member of this exact biome's fauna list
           (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/rosters/desert.json "fauna", 0.5) that was
           never wired — not invented; bodySize 0.15, and it is this mod's OWN def
           (mandrake.rut.patches, this file's own package), so no MayRequire is needed.
           The rest of the fix raises the grain already here (Kreetle/Sketto boosted
           below), same shape as the Gizka fix: no megafauna cut. Scavrat/WompRat/Rat
           were also boosted here at the time but were removed under
           EXTREME_DESERT_UNRULED_VERMIN_1 (2026-09-20 ruling: Fall-Line fauna are
           arrivals, not ambient biome fauna). -->
      <JOE_Landopus>0.5</JOE_Landopus>  <!-- landopus - small ambush predator, ruled, this mod's own def -->
      <RSW_Kreetle MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">1.3</RSW_Kreetle>  <!-- kreetle - ambush-small, keep; boosted from 0.8 for the ecosystem pyramid law -->
      <RSW_Jellypot MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.7</RSW_Jellypot>  <!-- jellypot - ambush-small, keep -->
      <RSW_Shyrack MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.6</RSW_Shyrack>  <!-- shyrack - ambush-flier, keep -->
      <RSW_Gorg MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.4</RSW_Gorg>  <!-- gorg - ambush-small, keep -->
      <RSW_Gutkurr MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.4</RSW_Gutkurr>  <!-- gutkurr - burst-predator, adjust-keep; interim stand-in, complemented (not replaced) by RSW_WraidAlpha, DESERT_BURST_PREDATOR_FLAGSHIP_1 -->
      <RSW_Jamel MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.4</RSW_Jamel>  <!-- Jamel - herd, keep -->
      <RSW_LongtailGorg MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.4</RSW_LongtailGorg>  <!-- longtail gorg - ambush-small, keep -->
      <RSW_Ronto MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.4</RSW_Ronto>  <!-- ronto - huge-herd, keep -->
      <RSW_Sketto MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.8</RSW_Sketto>  <!-- sketto - ambush-small, keep; boosted from 0.4 for the ecosystem pyramid law -->
      <RSW_Wraid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.4</RSW_Wraid>  <!-- wraid - burst-predator, adjust-keep; interim stand-in, complemented (not replaced) by RSW_WraidAlpha below, DESERT_BURST_PREDATOR_FLAGSHIP_1 -->
      <!-- DESERT_BURST_PREDATOR_FLAGSHIP_1: desert.md §4/§10's actual burst-predator
           flagship — a rarer, solitary reskin of RSW_Wraid carrying the staged
           RM_HeatDrivenBurst hediff (burst then heat-fatigue) and a retreat-to-shade
           comp reading RM_MapComponent_ShadeGrid.ShadeAt. Wraid and Gutkurr above stay
           as their own live entries (not removed — both remain legal, more common
           predators of this biome); this is the rare apex on top of them, not a
           replacement for either. -->
      <RSW_WraidAlpha MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.15</RSW_WraidAlpha>  <!-- alpha wraid - THE burst-predator flagship, rare apex -->
      <RSW_Sandstrider MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.4</RSW_Sandstrider>  <!-- desert ave - navigator, keep -->
      <RSW_Eopie MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Eopie>  <!-- eopie - herd, keep -->
      <RSW_Hrumph MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Hrumph>  <!-- hrumph - herd, import -->
      <RSW_IridonianReek MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_IridonianReek>  <!-- iridonian reek - herd, import -->
      <RSW_Jimvu MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Jimvu>  <!-- jimvu - herd, import -->
      <RSW_Kwi MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Kwi>  <!-- Kwi - herd, import -->
      <RSW_Skalder MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Skalder>  <!-- skalder - huge-herd, import -->
      <RSW_Uvak MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Uvak>  <!-- uvak - herd, import -->
      <RSW_Varactyl MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Varactyl>  <!-- varactyl - herd, import -->
      <RSW_Zeer MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Zeer>  <!-- zeer - herd, import -->
      <RSW_Falumpaset MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_Falumpaset>  <!-- falumpaset - herd, import -->
      <RSW_FrilledGorg MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_FrilledGorg>  <!-- frilled gorg - ambush-small, keep -->
      <RSW_Jakobeast MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_Jakobeast>  <!-- jakobeast - herd, import -->
      <RSW_Nerf MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_Nerf>  <!-- nerf - herd, keep -->
      <RSW_Nuna MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_Nuna>  <!-- nuna - herd-small, keep -->
      <RSW_Shaak MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_Shaak>  <!-- shaak - herd, import -->
      <RSW_TeeMuss MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_TeeMuss>  <!-- tee muss - herd, import -->
      <RSW_Worrt MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_Worrt>  <!-- worrt - ambush-small, keep -->
      <RSW_Spineroller MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_Spineroller>  <!-- needleroll - grain, keep -->
      <RSW_Bolotaur MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.1</RSW_Bolotaur>  <!-- bolotaur - herd, import -->
      <RSW_Clodhopper MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.1</RSW_Clodhopper>  <!-- clodhopper - ambush-small, keep -->
      <RSW_FeralGrazer MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.1</RSW_FeralGrazer>  <!-- feral grazer - herd, import -->
      <RSW_Gizka MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.1</RSW_Gizka>  <!-- gizka - ambush-small, keep -->
      <RSW_Iriaz MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.1</RSW_Iriaz>  <!-- iriaz - herd-small, keep -->
      <RSW_Krykna MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.1</RSW_Krykna>  <!-- krykna - ambush-small, keep -->
      <RSW_Runyip MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.1</RSW_Runyip>  <!-- runyip - herd, import -->
      <RSW_Voorpak MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.05</RSW_Voorpak>  <!-- voorpak - ambush-small, keep -->
      <RSW_Sandhorn MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.05</RSW_Sandhorn>  <!-- gigantelope - herd, keep -->
      <RSW_Dunestalker MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.05</RSW_Dunestalker>  <!-- sand prowler - ambush-burrow, keep -->
      <RSW_Ferroclaw MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.035</RSW_Ferroclaw>  <!-- terramorph - ambush-flat, keep -->
      <RSW_Sandmaw MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.025</RSW_Sandmaw>  <!-- sand squid - subsurface-slow, keep -->
      <RSW_Tuskcoil MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.015</RSW_Tuskcoil>  <!-- mammoth worm - subsurface-slow, keep -->
      <RSW_Horax MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.01</RSW_Horax>  <!-- horax - megafauna, import; interim stand-in, complemented (not replaced) by RSW_ShadeWhale below, COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1 -->
      <!-- COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1 (desert sheet): desert.md §4c/§10's actual
           filter-feeding shade-whale megafauna — a reskin of RSW_Horax's body/art,
           re-purposed herbivore/solitary, carrying RM_ShadeSeekingWanderExtension
           (real shade-seeking, DESERT_SHADE_GRID_KEYSTONE_1 infra). Sand
           filter-feeding itself is C#-owed (DESERT_SHADE_WHALE_FILTERFEED_1); the
           def lands now per desert.json's own "def can land first" note. Horax
           above stays wired as its own entry, same precedent as
           RSW_WraidAlpha/RSW_Wraid. -->
      <RSW_ShadeWhale MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.015</RSW_ShadeWhale>  <!-- shade whale - THE filter-feeding megafauna flagship -->
      <!-- DESERT_ROUND2_IMPORTS_UNLANDED_1 2026-09-20: round-2 import rows
           (rosters/desert.json "fauna", owner review 2026-09, commonality 0.5 each)
           wired for the first time. -->
      <RSW_Stoneback MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.5</RSW_Stoneback>  <!-- bokka - anywhere on the dayside, import -->
      <RSW_TruffleMole MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.5</RSW_TruffleMole>  <!-- truffle mole - sand burrower, desert & extreme desert, import -->
      <!-- AA_JOE_DESERT_PORT_BATCH_1 2026-09-20: the remaining round-2 import rows
           (design/Jawa/fauna/cast_assignment.csv, owner review 2026-09, commonality
           0.5 each) ported from scratch (RSW_GreatDevourer/RSW_Groundrunner/
           RSW_MatureFleshbeast, Defs/ThingDefs_Races) and wired for the first time.
           JOE_Cephalope is NOT a new port here - it was already absorbed verbatim
           (defName preserved) by STAT_NORM_WAVE2_RETIRE_1 on 2026-09-11, into this
           SAME mod (Defs/Absorbed_Cephaloids/Absorbed_Cephaloids_Defs.xml), and the
           donor mod (joe.cephaloids) was already removed from ModsConfig.xml that day
           - only its biome wiring here was ever owed, so no MayRequire guard is
           needed (same mod, unconditionally loaded together). -->
      <RSW_GreatDevourer MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.5</RSW_GreatDevourer>  <!-- great devourer - relative of the sarlacc, import -->
      <RSW_Groundrunner MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.5</RSW_Groundrunner>  <!-- groundrunner - desert, import -->
      <RSW_MatureFleshbeast MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.5</RSW_MatureFleshbeast>  <!-- mature fleshbeast - desert, immature sarlacc, import -->
      <JOE_Cephalope>0.5</JOE_Cephalope>  <!-- cephalope - sand burrower & swimmer, already absorbed & mod already retired (STAT_NORM_WAVE2_RETIRE_1) -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <RM_Leachmoss MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">1.5</RM_Leachmoss>  <!-- leachmoss: the fertile ground's fastest claimant, DESERT_LEACHMOSS_BUILD_1. Highest weight in this list on purpose (design §2b) — Gravel/Soil only (fertilityMin 0.5, never Sand), so it wins most rolls on ground it can take without ever competing with the ultracactus for sand. -->
      <RSW_Ultracactus MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.8</RSW_Ultracactus>  <!-- ultracactus: the buried canopy holding the open ground, DESERT_SIGNATURE_FLORA_1 -->
      <RUT_Vorrel MayRequire="mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora">0.1</RUT_Vorrel>  <!-- the cycle plant, DESERT_STAGGERSEED_BUILD_1. Lowest weight of the three desert plants on purpose: §4b puts it in "the protected water pockets" only, and its own fertilityMin 0.45 already keeps it off Sand, so this weight sets how thickly it fills the pockets it CAN take, not how far it spreads. Working name — see the header. -->
      <RM_Venomvine MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">0.25</RM_Venomvine>  <!-- the vine that holds territory by injury, §4b "the shade plants, which defend" — VENOMVINE_CONTACT_VENOM_BUILD_1. fertilityMin 0.5 already keeps it off Sand (the ultracactus's ground), so this weight sets how thickly it takes the patch ground it CAN reach, not how far it spreads. -->
      <RSW_Dunegrass MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.6</RSW_Dunegrass>  <!-- surra grass -->
      <RSW_Plant_Chakroot_Wild MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Plant_Chakroot_Wild>  <!-- wild chak-root plant -->
      <RSW_Plant_HubbaGourd_Wild MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_Plant_HubbaGourd_Wild>  <!-- wild hubba gourd plant -->
      <RSW_VellaraBloom MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.12</RSW_VellaraBloom>  <!-- vellara bloom -->
      <RSW_SweetbarkTree MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.06</RSW_SweetbarkTree>  <!-- dommo tree - tree -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>35</wildPlantRegrowDays>

    <!-- DESERT_PACK_ANIMALS_FOR_TRADERS_1 (owner, 2026-09-20: both deserts get traders).
         allowedPackAnimals was absent (= empty list), so PawnGroupKindWorker_Trader.
         CanGenerateFrom returned false and no trader caravan ever generated here.
         MEASURED: all five ported herd beasts carry <packAnimal>true</packAnimal> in
         their ThingDef (src/RimStarWars/SWBestiary/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RSW_{Bantha,
         Ronto,Eopie,Jamel,Falumpaset}.xml), so all five are listed. -->
    <allowedPackAnimals>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Bantha</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Ronto</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Eopie</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Jamel</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Falumpaset</li>
    </allowedPackAnimals>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
